## ✨ Overview

This project demonstrates the architecture behind an **AI-powered chat bot** — a Node.js/Express backend that talks to the **OpenAI API**, manages conversation state, and exposes a simple chat endpoint a frontend can call.

> 💬 User message → 🧠 Backend + OpenAI → 📤 AI response

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
┌────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐      ┌─────────────┐
│  Frontend  │ ───▶ │  Express Backend │ ───▶ │  OpenAI API │
│  (Chat UI) │ ◀─── │  (chat routes)   │ ◀─── │             │
└────────────┘      └──────────────────┘      └─────────────┘
                            │
                            ▼
                     ┌─────────────┐
                     │  Database   │
                     │ (chat logs, │
                     │  sessions)  │
                     └─────────────┘
```

*(Adjust this diagram to match your actual data flow — e.g., add caching, streaming, or a vector store for context/RAG.)*

## 🚀 Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 💬 Chat Endpoint | Accepts a user message and returns an AI-generated reply |
| 🧵 Conversation History | Maintains context across a session |
| 🔑 API Key Management | Keeps OpenAI credentials secure via environment variables |
| ⚡ Streaming *(optional)* | Streams tokens back to the client as they're generated |
| 🗂️ Session Storage | Persists chat history *(in-memory, DB, or Redis — update to match yours)* |

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Runtime:** Node.js 18+
- **Framework:** Express 4.x
- **AI Provider:** OpenAI API (e.g., `gpt-4o` / `gpt-4o-mini` — update to your model)
- **Storage:** In-memory / MongoDB / Redis *(update to your actual choice)*

